            <ArticleTitle>[The spontaneous intramurale rupture of the oesophagus: case report of a rare oesophageal lesion].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1172-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous intramural rupture of the oesophagus is a rare cause of acute pain in the chest and upper abdomen. A case of spontaneous intramural oesophageal rupture in an 82-year-old woman is reported. Symptoms, diagnostic investigation, aetiology and therapy of the lesion were demonstrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
